PUPPET WORKSHOP -- CLASSIFICATION OF PUPPET TECHNIQUES
Puppet Brigade reference

The Brigade classifies its arts by control complexity and lawfulness. This sheet
guides instructors in what may be taught and to whom.

Class I -- Basic animation: single-puppet control, up to ten chakra threads.
Taught to all Brigade trainees.
Class II -- Multi-puppet control: several puppets at once, coordinated attack and
capture combinations (the Crow-and-Black-Ant method). Chunin Brigade and above.
Class III -- Mass control: the legendary hundred-puppet command attributed to the
defector Sasori. Studied in theory only; no living member is cleared to attempt
it at scale.
Class IV -- FORBIDDEN, Human Puppetry: the conversion of a slain body into a
puppet, retaining its chakra and techniques. Pioneered and abused by Sasori,
including his puppet of the Third Kazekage. Strictly outlawed; sealed manuals,
Kazekage authorization only, for study of countermeasures alone.

Poison integration applies across all classes and is governed by the Poison
Division. Maintained under Brigade seal.
